Fixes: 7c87942aef52 ("wm97xx_battery: Use irq to detect charger state")
Signed-off-by: Waqar Hameed <waqar.hameed@axis.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/97b55f0479a932eea7213844bf66f28a974e27a2.1766270196.git.waqar.hameed@axis.com
Signed-off-by: Sebastian Reichel <sebastian.reichel@collabora.com>

Here is the root cause:
The IRQ handler for the charge GPIO is registered before the power supply structure is allocated and registered. If an interrupt occurs between `request_irq()` and `power_supply_register()`, the handler calls `power_supply_changed()` with an uninitialized (NULL) pointer, leading to a NULL pointer dereference.

